# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project follows [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

## [Unreleased]

### Added

- Nothing yet.

---

## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-02

### Added

- Telegram-based backup management interface.
- English and Persian user interfaces.
- Role-based access with `SUPERADMIN` and `ADMIN` roles.
- Backup profile creation, editing, execution, and monitoring.
- Manual backup execution.
- One-time schedules.
- Interval schedules.
- Daily, weekly, and monthly schedules.
- Five-field Cron scheduling.
- Configurable Backup Timezone with UTC persistence.
- PostgreSQL backup support.
- MySQL and MariaDB backup support.
- Microsoft SQL Server backup support.
- SQLite backup support.
- Local file and directory backups.
- Remote file and directory backups over SSH.
- Local GitLab native backup support.
- Remote GitLab backup support.
- Trusted remote-server management.
- SSH host-key fingerprint verification and pinning.
- Private-key SSH authentication.
- Archive and compression pipeline.
- Age-based backup encryption.
- SHA-256 artifact verification.
- Original backup size and final artifact size tracking.
- Multipart Telegram delivery for large backup artifacts.
- Durable backup runs, artifacts, and delivery state.
- Durable retry scheduling.
- Restart-safe worker recovery.
- Artifact retention and cleanup handling.
- Runtime health and component status reporting.
- Audit logging.
- Structured application logging.
- PostgreSQL-backed application state.
- Alembic database migrations.
- Docker Compose deployment.
- Dedicated backup worker service.
- Dedicated Local GitLab helper service.
- Production installation, security, and operations documentation.

### Changed

- Separated the Telegram Bot control plane from the backup Worker data plane.
- Local filesystem backup mounts are now accessible only by the Worker.
- Local source Create/Edit validation now uses a restricted Unix-domain validation interface between Bot and Worker.
- Local GitLab backups use a dedicated helper-only architecture.
- Docker socket access is restricted to the GitLab Helper.
- Backup scheduling is independent of the host operating-system timezone.
- Backup run configuration is persisted as an immutable snapshot.
- Telegram delivery is serialized through a single managed Worker transport owner.
- Local and remote GitLab acquisition paths use verified staging before further processing.

### Fixed

- Fixed Telegram delivery recovery after temporary SOCKS5 proxy or network outages.
- Fixed Telethon client reuse after fatal background transport failures.
- Added safe client retirement and recreation after unusable Telegram connections.
- Fixed startup behavior so temporary Telegram connectivity failure does not prevent the Worker scheduler from running.
- Fixed durable delivery retry behavior after Worker restarts.
- Fixed retry handling for partially completed multipart deliveries.
- Fixed exhausted delivery attempts during operator retry.
- Fixed stale delivery checkpoints after lease ownership changes.
- Fixed retention cleanup races with retry and purge operations.
- Fixed repeated retries of invalid finalized-artifact metadata.
- Fixed final-artifact durability before manifest publication.
- Fixed GitLab Helper socket cleanup after timeout or cancellation.
- Fixed unobserved completed Worker task exceptions.
- Fixed Telethon session-path aliasing.
- Fixed Local GitLab helper permission handling.
- Fixed runtime directory ownership and permission handling.
- Fixed multiple scheduling and recovery edge cases discovered during production hardening.

### Security

- Removed direct local backup-source filesystem mounts from the Telegram Bot.
- Added restricted Worker-side validation for local source paths.
- Added approved-root confinement for local filesystem sources.
- Added traversal and symlink-escape protections.
- Preserved acquisition-time revalidation to reduce TOCTOU risk.
- Restricted the Local GitLab Docker socket to the GitLab Helper.
- Hardened GitLab Helper operations to an allowlisted command set.
- Added SSH fingerprint pinning for trusted remote servers.
- Added encrypted storage for sensitive credentials.
- Reduced secret exposure in logs, exceptions, tracebacks, and diagnostics.
- Added safe subprocess output limits.
- Hardened runtime file and directory permissions.
- Added repository hygiene rules for sessions, runtime data, secrets, logs, and backup artifacts.
- Added dependency and static-security validation.
- Updated production dependencies following security review.

### Reliability

- Added bounded exponential delivery retry with jitter.
- Added transient versus permanent Telegram failure classification.
- Added recovery after SOCKS5 proxy interruption.
- Added restart-safe delivery continuation.
- Preserved successfully delivered multipart parts during retries.
- Prevented source backup acquisition from being repeated solely because Telegram delivery failed.
- Added Worker-side source validation availability checks.
- Added durable run and artifact recovery.
- Added additional filesystem and artifact verification before cleanup.

### Documentation

- Rewritten `README.md`.
- Added `INSTALLATION.md`.
- Added `SECURITY.md`.
- Added `OPERATIONS.md`.
- Added `AUDIT_REPORT.md`.
- Documented Docker deployment and runtime directory preparation.
- Documented Local GitLab helper architecture.
- Documented Local Files / Directories Worker-only mount architecture.
- Documented Telegram proxy configuration and delivery recovery.
- Documented safe upgrades, migrations, backup, restore, troubleshooting, and destructive reset procedures.

### Testing

- Expanded the automated test suite to more than 500 tests.
- Added Telegram transport failure and recovery tests.
- Added durable delivery restart tests.
- Added Local Files / Directories validation protocol tests.
- Added Bot/Worker mount-isolation tests.
- Added GitLab helper tests.
- Added scheduler and timezone regression coverage.
- Added PostgreSQL, MySQL/MariaDB, MSSQL, SSH, filesystem, and crash-recovery integration coverage.
- Added Compose configuration validation.
- Added Ruff, mypy, Bandit, compilation, migration-head, and whitespace validation.

